Dark Souls 3 is finally gracing consoles  and PCs everywhere but unfortunately  ashen ones playing on their personal  computers have run into some trouble if  you've experienced early game crashes  here's the good news a steam user by the  name of Alya Dan Ward has found a  temporary fix according to ward the  crashes are caused by a lighting glitch  which triggers as you approach a bonfire  to avoid this your best bet is to drop  the lighting option to its lowest  possible setting alternatively you can  make your character wear a helmet  although the only way to do this so  early in the game is to start with the  night class these solutions aren't  guaranteed to work but at this point  they're definitely your best option  these are only temporary solutions but  publisher Namco Bandai is aware of the  problem and is reportedly working on a  permanent fix hopefully those of you who  encountered the crash will get to  experience Dark Souls 3 for what it  truly is after all we did give it an 8  out of 10 in the meantime you can stick  with GameSpot for all the Dark Souls  news you need
 

